"""ATLASZ AURÓRA V7.3 - catalogue of PLANNED modules / EXTEND tasks / DEFERRED projects (RECORDS ONLY).

Every entry here describes something that does NOT exist as working code yet (or is an extension of an existing
component). Nothing in this file is a claim that the module exists. `kind`:
  NEW       - a new module that must be built (status PLANNED)
  EXTEND    - missing function(s) to be added to an EXISTING component (status of the host stays; the gap is tracked here)
  DEFERRED  - owner-deferred future project (PLANNED_DEFERRED, not activated, hours not committed)
  DECISION  - an owner decision is needed before any work can be scheduled
Matching: `ids` are exact keys (ATL-REQ-nnnn, <src>-L<line>, V73-Snn-nnn, ATLASZ-xx-nnn); ranges "a..b" allowed for
ATL-REQ numbers and for directive lines ("01a0d7b8-L553..560"). `rx` is a regular expression applied (case-insensitive)
to  text + planned_module_hint  of directive items that are still unmatched after the exact keys.
`rel` = names of EXISTING components (v1 names) the module relates to / must be wired to.
Hours are ESTIMATES (implementation, verification) in engineer-hours; they are planning figures, not measurements.
"""

